{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:9f7d62a8e6157b1c","name":"Fiber Cord","source":{"id":"source:reference-9f7d62a8e6157b1c","title":"Fiber Cord","revision":26291,"timestamp":"2025-03-15T21:15:45Z","sha256":"ffe0a7d7490e40f0f640380f7590db8d702dd0ef4e981575be7984cfb5690fd0","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26291","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Fiber%20Cord&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-9f7d62a8e6157b1c","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One end of this small cord of metal fibers attaches to the hilt of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},". The other end is attached to a piece of armor or a metal gauntlet, making it more difficult to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disarm"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disarm","referenceId":"reference:0449aa195af99b14"}," the wielder. When the wielder of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," with a Fiber Cord is ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disarmed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disarmed"},", the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disarming"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disarming"}," character cannot catch the weapon (or call it to their hand, if using ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Disarm"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Disarm","referenceId":"reference:c1aff7feafa6c9d3"}]},"). The weapon is still considered \"dropped\" and the wielder must spend an action to pick it up, though it hangs by its Fiber Cord until the wielder does so.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
